Yes, I'll agree with that any time.  It's a problem that won't go away
anytime soon. I think it's getting worse.  (That must be a sign of
oldness.)

There have been some fairly unbiased side-by-side comparisons of
productivity with C vs. Ada, at various programmer skill levels.  Ada
comes out ahead, usually by a large margin.  It seems to take a bit longer
to write, but much less time to debug.

In the modern world, where bugs don't matter, Ada is at a disadvantage.

