re: switch / case:

I have had occasions where I did make use of the lack of automatic "break" at
the end of a case statement.

Think of a dishwasher:


switch(wash_type)
{
	case heavy_duty:
					fill_tank();
					wash(5 minutes, no_spoap, no_rinse_agent);
					empty_tank();
	case very_dirty:
					fill_tank();
					wash(5 minutes, no_spoap, no_rinse_agent);
					empty_tank();
	case regular:
					fill_tank();
					wash(10 minutes, spoap, no_rinse_agent);
					empty_tank();
					
	case rinse:		
					fill_tank();
					wash(10 minutes, no_spoap, rinse_agent);
					empty_tank();
					dryer(15 minutes);
					break;

	case rinse_only:
					fill_tank();
					wash(5 minutes, no soap, no rinse agent);
					empty_tank();
					break;

	case dish_warmer:
					dryer(5 minutes);
					break;



So, in the case of a heavy_duty wash, it will fall down all the way to the end
of the rinse and then stop.


