The TMB11 was a Unibus controller for the old 800 bpi TU10 tape drives.
It was presented as a "system unit" which could be mounted in the standard

PDP11 BA-style boxes, which distinguished it from it's predecessor, the
TM11, which had to mounted outside of the box.  It was a DEC product
that used the old M7821 Interrupt Control module, M795 WC and CA
module, and the M796 Bus Control module.  These three modules were
used on just about all of the DEC peripheral controllers back in those
days,
which, incidentally, I recall as being pre-late 70's - maybe '74 or '75.

