> |>         3. BREAK.  Break should be allowed from ALL Begin/End ({})
> |>            constructs (including IF ELSE).  You should also be able to
> |>            BREAK # where # is the number of Begin/End blocks you want
> |>            to break out of.
> 
> Sounds like you want GOTO back.  I thought Dyjkstra convinced everyone
> that was a bad idea??  ;-)

Not quite.  GOTOs can go backwards as well as forwards making a mess out
of the program's flow.  BREAKs can only go forward.  Dyjkstra was
commenting on certain abuses of GOTO.

However, even with just going forward, I don't like BREAK since the
reader of the code doesn't know where the BREAK will go.  Sure, you can
look and 'guess', but only the compiler knows for sure.  And adding
another level of BEGIN/END makes you go and visit all the enclosed
BREAKs and increment their "level".

Thats why I actually like forward GOTOs.  You get to name and SEE the
label in the source code.

BLISS has a LEAVE statement and named-block.  You give a name to block
and say LEAVE with that name.  Its always a forward branch and you don't
have to worry about other BEGIN/ENDs being added.
