One thing about C:

I find that I don't entirely trust the C compiler. As a result, when I do
anything where I have any doubts on how the compiler will react, I will test
the module extensively to ensure it works reliably.

If someone blindly trusts the compiler, then that person is beggging for
problems in C. But if you don't trust the compiler and test everything, you
probably end up with more robust programs.


