Elaine Poulsen (elainep@excitehome.net) wrote:
: Where can I buy the 300W 3.3V AT powersupply that will work with my
: motherboard.
: I'm confused as many things I've read lead me to believe it requires a
: special power
: supply to work.
: Any help or information would greatly be appreciated.

I've had luck with a power supply I bought from Computer Surplus
Outlet.  Go to http://www.computersurplusoutlet.com and look up part #
CAS-30033.  It's $99, but it's what you need and it's the only place I
know where you can buy it.

Just a couple of warnings if you do buy this PS:  When you install it,
double check the four power supply connectors on the motherboard and make
sure that you haven't swapped the 3.3V connectors.  None of the connectors
are keyed, so it's very easy to hook it up wrong.  Email me if you need
help with this.  Also, the power supply does not have a power switch, it
expects the signal from the motherboard which the PC64 does not
provide.  You have to add your own SPST switch across the black and green
wires.
