Oliver Kr�tzschmar <oliver.kraetzschmar@T-Online.de> wrote

> Inside I found 4 memory modules with 4 x 9 chips (HYB514100BJ-70).
> One was loose and there was one sslot empty between this module
> and the other 3 modules.
> I removed the modules and put them back starting from the rear, but
> nothing happened. Even iIf I remove all the memory I get the same results.

The memory must go in a set of four. First in slots 0a,0b,0c & 0d and then
if you get additional memory in 1e,1f,1g & 1h. Each set of four must contain
identical simms either 4MB or 16MB. They cannot be mixed within sets.
Therefore you have a minimum RAM of 16MB . Also if you have a 16MB set and a
4MB set the 4MB simms must be installed in the 0 slots.

Are you sure about that error code? I ran a search on the /90 service manual
and although 1111 xxxx is the format for boot time LEDs there is no 0010
code listed.

I'm afraid there was no diagram so you'll have to look for the slot
markings.

Hope this helps a bit

Cheers

Dave







