our own warnings) found hundreds of warnings caused by some header files in
/usr/include/io/cam.
Here are a few typical ones (they are all caused by using "unsigned char"
bit fields, which is not nice - they should be "int" or "unsigned int"):

cc: Warning: /usr/include/io/cam/rzdisk.h, line 178: In the declaration of
"perfdt", the bitfield type is not an int, signed int or unsigned int.
    u_char      perfdt:5,       /* Peripheral Device Type             */
----------------^

cc: Warning: /usr/include/io/cam/cdrom.h, line 201: In the declaration of
"ps_lbamsf", the bitfield type is not an int, signed int or unsigned int.
        u_char  ps_lbamsf       : 1,    /* Address format 0/1 = LBA/MSF */
----------------^

cc: Warning: /usr/include/io/cam/scsi_all.h, line 83: In the declaration of
"save", the bitfield type is not an int, signed int or unsigned int.
