Newer DEC/Compaq C compilers have a feature that will suppress
disgnostics in system header files or other directories where
you can not easily make changes. See the -SD option in the cc(1)
man page.

If this feature is not yet available in your system compiler, you
can upgrade your compiler in Tru64 UNIX V4.0D and later using the
Developers' Toolkit Supplement. It is available on the web at:

  http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/dtk/

All that is needed is an active Developers' Toolkit license in
oder to install/run it on your V4.0D or later machine. You may
also need a 'cc' driver patch for V4.0D or V4.0E. This is described
in the Installation Guide on the web.

You will find newer features and better optimization in the new
compiler. It will also default to -std (Relaxed ANSI) mode, which
may be a change for some V4.0x users.

If you need more info, let me know.

-Jeff


