The thing I always liked about DECnet was it's scale of economy. DECnet is
very frugal with network bandwidth.

When one system wanted to talk to another system in the same DECnet area,
and providing you had set up a Level 1 router, the system that wanted to
talk would always kindly ask the router what the address was of the target.
When leaving your area, then the system would always ask the Level 2 router.

None of this noisy broadcasting going on.

LAT is a great protocol, it really enabled all kinds of cool things to
happen, not just a little bit of Terminal Traffic.

rtt




