DEC/Compaq has always charged for license upgrades when doing CPU upgrades,
even when in the same box.  Ever upgraded a 6000-200 to a 6000-300, or
added processors to a 6000-600?  They usually have offered a bundled
hardware/software upgrade package at a significant discount when new models 
came out, but you still had to pay.  You can argue with this policy, but 
they certainly have a right to do it.  I don't think it has anything to 
do with the hardware design or internal upgradeability of any given system.
Even if they made a CPU upgrade for the DS10 that was just a CPU chip-swap,
they would probably still charge you for a VMS license upgrade, and maybe
