Not really.  Typical motherboards cost $200 and new CPU $500 (plus or
minus), so if you can reuse your memory and other components (which you
usually can, at least for one upgrade) you can double the speed of a system
for roughly $500-700, depending upon whether or not a motherboard is
needed.  The equivalent "upgrade" price for a DS10, 466->600, is nearly 10
times higher. Heck, you can throw out and buy a new PC, with all new
components, and that will still be .lt. 1/2 the cost of a DS10 upgrade. 

