Uh, no. The issue is that the CPU is soldered to the motherboard. You
can't swap the 466MHz CPU for the 616 MHz (or whatever it is) flavor
because you'd have to use a soldering iron and you'd probably ruin
something in the process (that is, assuming that they have allowed
various clock frequencies to be adjusted - which I assume that they
