use of the soldering iron to swap parts to do the upgrade). Or, of course,
you could swap out the entire motherboard - but is there such a board
swap upgrade available? I think not.

I also think that incrementing the model numbers by 5 rather than 1 is
silly. What comes next? The post DS15 model presumably isn't going to
be a DS20. If they increment half way again, that'd make it the DS17.5.
Having the followup to the DS25 be a DS30 would also be silly - it would
imply that it could support 3 CPUs instead of 2 (based on how the numbering
scheme currently works), so do we then get the DS27.5 as well? (And so
on, through the rest of the models.)

