  Most licenses have other requirements for more permanent transfers.

:Given two nearly identical AlphaServer 1200's, if one dies
:can it's hard drives be simply moved to the other machine and then booted up
:without any significant action other than perhaps running an AUTOGEN?

  For various definitions of "nearly identical", yes.  

  Assuming the OpenVMS version supports the target platform, you will
  be able BACKUP/IMAGE and boot and use OpenVMS on it -- at worst, you 
  will have to perform a conversational bootstrap and a "USE DEFAULT" 
  to reset the system parameters, followed by an AUTOGEN pass, followed 
  by hunting down all of the device-specific references scattered through
  your environment (if there are configuration differences).  (Once you 
  hunt these references a couple of times, you will hopefully start to 
  learn the value of using logical names and eschewing physical device 
  names where possible.)

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
