After discovering the interpretation of the ASC/ASCQ pair which pointed to
a failing disk, and noting that the error log entries *did not* contain any
associated port/target info, I preferred all of the disks to the other
controller (this is a redundant pair). The errors continued; and the new
error log entries *did* contain port/target info. Disk was replaced; and then
replaced again. Errors continued. Disk was moved to another slot in the
Storage Works cabinet... no more errors. Diagnosis: bad slot on shelf.

