Since the HSZxx controllers don't support SCS they can't send non-disk specific
errors.  They tend to
tag the error onto the next I/O request it sees.  You will see this when the
controller does a SCSI port reset.

If these errors are isolates to only drives on one controller I would suspect the
controller.  It may also be a problem with the host to controller interface.

Regards,

Cass

