>Another question: are OpenVMS licenses tied to a specific machine or are
>they portable?

All OpenVMS layered product license are "redesignatable", meaning that they
can be transferred from one system to another, equivalent (in the same tier)
system within a legal entity (same company).  Redesignating a license to a
higher tier system requires an upgrade license.

Operating systems and System-Integrated products, as well as a list of other
products like DECserver software, DECbridge microcode, HSx software,
PrintServer software, and VXT software, are relicensable, meaning that, for
a fee, Compaq will cancel a license and reissue a new one for that product.
VMScluster and DECnet licenses are noth relicensable and redesignatable.
Relicensing can be between legal entities.
