>Alan Winston - SSRL Admin Cmptg Mgr wrote:
>> LANCP> show device esa0/param
>> 
>> Device Parameters ESA0:
>>              Value  Parameter
>>              -----  ---------
>>             Normal  Controller mode
>>           External  Internal loopback mode
>>  08-00-2B-BE-EE-69  Hardware LAN address
>>            CSMA/CD  Communication medium
>>                 32  Minimum receive buffers
>>                 32  Maximum receive buffers
>>                 No  Full duplex enable
>>                 No  Full duplex operational
>>        Unspecified  Line media
>>                 10  Line speed (megabits/second)
>
>Thanks for this tip!  Very handy.  And here all along I thought the above
>parameters referred to the console setting, not necessarily the adapter's
>capabilities.
>
>> Good luck!  (And, incidentally, thanks for Hypermail!)
>
>My pleasure!  This is an app I wrote for a task which evaporated before I had
>finished.  At least somebody got some use out of it. (:-) Are you still using
>it, or have you switched to YAHMAIL?

I'm (still) using Hypermail to serve out a mailing-list archive where the
subject-line search is important; I'm using yahMAIL to make personal VMS mail
stores available to their owners over the web.  I find them both useful.  (I
tweaked hypermail slightly to suppress display of all the "received" etc 
internet headers.  Fortran was my first langugage so I love FORTRAN CGI
programming.)

-- Alan

