Jonathan McCormack wrote:
> 
> One of our clients wants to stop using LAT & DECNET on their network.  Is it
> possible to disable LAT and DECNET on a Decserver 90 and use just TCP/IP for
> terminal connections?

Terminal Servers don't use DECnet. For proof, note the inablity to set a
DECnet address on the server itself. You can assign one in NCP on a VMS
host (DECnet Phase-IV); but that is entirely unnecessary and server
never sees it.

You can use only the TCP/IP and simply disable transparent bridging on
your brouters. That will restrict any LAT broadcasts to the LAN segments
where the termianl servers live.

