In alt.sys.pdp11 Tony Scandora <scandora@cmt.anl.gov> wrote:
> The 11/73 used the Q bus for memory.  The 11/93 and /94, and maybe the 11/83
> and /84 did not use the Q or UNIBUS for memory.  If my memory serves me
> correctly, it was called Private Memory Interconnect (PMI).  I do not know
> if this was the same memory bus as the MicroVAX II's.

PMI uses the same physical connections as a Q-bus, in fact it just uses
the CD slots on any Q-bus backplane that has "straight" rather than
"serpentine" layout.  It's not at all similar to the microVAX memory bus,
which is carried over separate ribbon cables.

