Dan,

You won't be able to run dual CPUs with the main logic board
identified by the DECpc XLl 590 Version 1.23 BIOS.  To run dual CPUs,
you need to replace it with the DEC part number 54-23606 main logic
board, the board used in a Celebris XL.  Then you'll be able to run
133MHz (2/1 bus clock multiplier) or 100MHz (3/2) Pentium CPUs.
You'll also need a little tiny board to attach to the CPU card to
enable the support for the second processor.

Another CPU card, 54-24490, supports up to dual Pentium 166s, when
installed in the same 54-23606, of course.

We have a dwindling supply of these parts still available... Ben Myers

