news:MuAh6.9403$zz4.232837@news2-win.server.ntlworld.com...
> One of our clients wants to stop using LAT & DECNET on their network.  Is
it
> possible to disable LAT and DECNET on a Decserver 90 and use just TCP/IP
for
> terminal connections?
>

The LAT software on the DECserver cannot be turned off.  It only kicks in
when a connect request at the Local> prompt is issued.  The way you get rid
of LAT on your network is to simply not run the LAT startup on your OpenVMS
systems.  With no LAT hosts, the terminal server will have no where to go.

Mike
Former OpenVMS LAT developer




