You may have to use LANCP to force those adapters to full duplex, if it's 
possible.  (The 3000-300 LX I'm on right now says:

LANCP> show device esa0/param

Device Parameters ESA0:
             Value  Parameter
             -----  ---------
            Normal  Controller mode
          External  Internal loopback mode
 08-00-2B-BE-EE-69  Hardware LAN address
           CSMA/CD  Communication medium
                32  Minimum receive buffers
                32  Maximum receive buffers
                No  Full duplex enable
                No  Full duplex operational
       Unspecified  Line media
                10  Line speed (megabits/second)


In any case, I've had fairly bad luck with auto-negotiation between Cisco 
switches and Digital adapters.  Why don't you try using LANCP to force the
adapters to full duplex and disable auto-negotiation on the Cabletron switch
to make it full duplex - that'll at least tell you for sure whether full duplex
works on the 3000s.)

Good luck!  (And, incidentally, thanks for Hypermail!)

