In article <95505v$3gm138@imsp212.netvigator.com>, <tfhkcyt2000@taifuji.com> writes:
:    I have heared that DPWS 500AU can run tru64 unix but DPWS 500A 
:can not, is it true ? and can you tell me where is the difference
:between DPWS 500AU and DPWS 500A ?

  The -a series officially targets (only) Microsoft Windows NT, and was 
  supported and licensed (only) for Windows NT.

  You might find yourself able to boot OpenVMS or Tru64 UNIX on the -a 
  series, and you might not.  Some of the systems will -- though not 
  supported -- probably be able to boot and run OpenVMS or Tru64 UNIX, 
  once you get SRM loaded and running.  That said, other members of the 
  -a series will have various hardware limits that can (will) prevent 
  OpenVMS or Tru64 UNIX from running.  (Even within one model of the
  series, there can be hardware differences -- see the discussion in 
  the FAQ around the Intel SIO vs the Cypress.  The OpenVMS -au boxes
  received the Cypress hardware...)

  If you choose to attempt this, you will also have to confirm that all 
  I/O widgets installed in the -a or -au system are supported by OpenVMS 
  or Tru64 UNIX.

  I will assume this is a hobbyist system, other licenses probably are
  not valid for use on this system given its (lack of) formal OpenVMS
  or Tru64 UNIX support for the -a series platform.

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com



