  More properly (for ease of searching), this is the VRT19-HA.

:...

  Please see the OpenVMS FAQ sections:

SUPP4.  Can I reuse old keyboards, mice and monitors with a PC?
SUPP5.  Which video monitor works with which graphics controller?

:...Sorry, VAXes are new to me, so please help me....

  The processor -- the DECstation 5000 series processor is MIPS and not 
  VAX, BTW -- is not particularly relevent to the question of monitors 
  and graphics controller compatibility.  Display capability is almost
  always independent of the computer processor, depending centrally on 
  the graphics controller and the monitor.  (The OpenVMS FAQ goes into 
  some detail here, too.)

  The OpenVMS FAQ is available at various sites, including:

    www.openvms.compaq.com

  Deja.com will also likely have discussions, as most monitors get 
  discussed fairly regularly.

  Specific details: the VRT19-HA (Northern Hemisphere) and -H4 (Southern
  Hemisphere) are dual-scan and auto-sense, supporting 70.70 KHz horizontal 
  and 66 Hz vertical at 1280 by 1024, and 77.17 KHz horizontal and 72 Hz 
  vertical at 1280 by 1024.

