No, uVAXII memory cards use the Qbus CD slots to assert the memory
address bits. There are no Qbus bus cycles. The ribbon cable connector
carries the data bytes in and out, 32 bits plus parity at a time,
between the CPU and the memory.

In a full AB-CD back plane (9275-S ??) it should be possible to build a
RAM disk controller that *does* sit on the Qbus and uses the uVAX
memory cards as it's array.

Yes, I have pondered doing this.  8-)

Jeff Campbell

