> I've always wondered: What is the difference between a Northern
> Hemisphere monitor and a Southern Hemisphere one?

For a monochrome monitor, there is no difference. For a color monitor, the
tube is inverted because the magnetic field is inverted inthe southern
hemisphere. If you take your North America color monitor and invert it, you
will likely see some color distortions. Down under it would distort if not
inverted.


