> flex   cflex.l && mv lex.yy.c cflex.c
> "cflex.l", line 66: illegal character
> "cflex.l", line 68: unknown error processing section 1
> "cflex.l", line 406: undeclared start condition IDENT
> *** Exit 1
> Stop.
> -----------------

> Here are lines 66, 68 and 406 of cflex.l:
> %option noyywrap              <- line 66
> %o 30000                      <- line 68
> <IDENT>{id}            {      <- line 406

> Could some lex-master enlighten enlighten me?  I believe that I am using
> GNU flex-2.5.4, but not positive.

OSF1/.../Tru64 has a rather old version of flex.  The %option is a flex
extension (2.5.4's manpage indicates that it is not a POSIX feature),
and probably does not appear in that version of flex.  Notwithstanding
the limitations of this version of flex, CFengine is not POSIX:

       If you do not supply your own version  of  yywrap(),  then
       you  must  either  use %option noyywrap (in which case the
       scanner behaves as though yywrap()  returned  1),  or  you
       must  link  with -lfl to obtain the default version of the
       routine, which always returns 1.

