  Not offhand. There is no published external-to-Q mapping of 2-5-2 style
numbers back to the option name (which, in this case, is probably MS<some-
thing>.

  Even the former in-house "bible" (the Option Module Summary) only listed
the option name or M-series number for boards, not the 2-5-2.

  In the old days, you could call Part Number Assistance and ask them for
the "used-on" info for a 2-5-2. They had stacks and stacks of fiche that
they would scan for this data. But I think that group has been phased out.

  BTW, also in the old days, it was useful to know both the 2-5-2 and the
model, as one was almost always a lot cheaper than the other, but you could
never tell which was cheaper - SCSI cables being a prime example. Sometimes
the 2-5-2 was cheaper, sometimes the B-series was cheaper. Of course, not
all of them were orderable as 2-5-2's.

